12. Leap Year
Logic

A leap year follows these rules:

If a year is divisible by 400, it is a leap year.
Otherwise, if it is divisible by 4 but not divisible by 100, it is also a leap year.
Otherwise, it is not.

year % 400 == 0 ||
(year % 4 == 0 && year % 100 != 0)
This means:

Either the year is divisible by 400,
OR it is divisible by 4 but not by 100.

If either rule is satisfied, it's a leap year.

import java.util.Scanner;
public class LeapYear {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int year = sc.nextInt();
        if ((year % 400 == 0) || (year % 4 == 0 && year % 100 != 0))
            System.out.println("Leap Year");
        else
            System.out.println("Not Leap Year");
    }
}

